  "body": "### Summary\nAs the AQ write flow's author, I want the refusals the local AQ capture left out, so that the app does not guess them. Extends the method of #574; #591 already holds the addition after the flood limit, this issue holds the rest.\n\n### Scope\nFrom a **local** instance of `toyo@96c0aea` only, never the live service (same method as #574):\n- a comment over the column length;\n- a non-ASCII value in `nom`, `topic_titre` or `commentaire`;\n- a topic or post number that is not numeric;\n- an existing AQ id with a missing field.\n\nThe live host's own headers are not in this scope: no fixture holds them and no refusal may be sent to the live host to get them. A read's headers need the operator's go first.\n\n### Sources\n`docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md`, LOT-055 \"Refusal answers of a local instance\". `aq/api/addAlerte.php` @ `toyo@96c0aea`. The kit's `AQ local check` accepts the run's forms only, so a new value form is added to `tooling/fixtures/anonymize.py` with its test.\n\n### Wanted by\n#81 (LOT-055 create), #224 (LOT-134).\n\n### Acceptance criteria\nAnonymized `origin: local-instance` fixtures committed (`response_headers`, and `body_length` for an empty answer), manifest and protocol entry updated, the *pending capture* mark removed.\n",
